lf-contract 0.1
# sha-rotr is an IR 0.2 word (src/program/sha-words.fs uses LSHIFT and
# -ROT): leanforth verify refuses it, since its receipt needs schema 0.4,
# which awaits the owner's [format] gate (plan 8.4.1k). Contract language
# 0.1 has no rotation either; what the word computes, FIPS 180-4's ROTR, is
# proved by Lean (shaRotr_correct in tests/reference/program-ir.lean) and
# its export re-checked by LeanForth (make reference-program-sha-export).
# This contract states only the range of the result. No expect line: the
# outcome is the refusal, not one of the generator's.
id sha-rotr/0
word sha-rotr
ir tests/program/ir/sha-words.ir
stack ( u n -- u' )
inputs u n
statement For a 32-bit word u and 0 < n < 32 the word returns a 32-bit word (FIPS 180-4's ROTR^n(u), which this contract language cannot state).
pre 0 <= u && u <= 4294967295
pre 0 < n && n < 32
case true
  out r
  ensure 0 <= r && r <= 4294967295
